<!--
  ARCHIVED PROBE — head CSS canary (archived 2026-08-18, user decision;
  supersedes the same-day permanent-instrument call after the CSS-cliff
  round closed green).

  What it measured, all verdicts recorded in MJML-AUTHORING-GUIDE §2b-bis:
  - Gmail drops the ENTIRE head stylesheet past 16,384 delivered <style>
    bytes, on every Gmail surface (pair 5BTkRd 27,126B all-dead /
    XK3793 487B all-honoured).
  - EN ingests a CSS-type replacement once per <style> wrapper — a nested
    wrapper DOUBLED every delivered head (24,952B) until the block html
    carried the tag bare (13,325B, TlHVjaQ…).
  - Acceptance PASS 2026-08-18 (TlHVjaQ…): bar 1 GREEN on Gmail Android
    and Gmail web, light and dark; mobile bar blue on phones; desktop bar
    purple on webmail; dark bar firing on Android. Outlook bar 1 is
    always red — Word ignores media queries; expected, not a failure.

  To re-measure Gmail: paste this block into BOTH catalogs (it lived in
  mjml_all-blocks and tpl_unified-blocks under Utilities), re-import,
  re-upload, send through EoA. It carries data-probe (signal colors stay
  out of the palette census and color audit) and an import-exclude
  wrapper (never ships in a real send unless deliberately overridden).
-->

    <!-- START: Probe Block (head CSS canary) -->
    <!-- PERMANENT INSTRUMENT (2026-08-18, guide §2b-bis): four canary bars
         that make a real send's head-CSS survival visible per client. Bar 1's
         rule hides inside the always-true max-width:9999px wrapper because EN
         INLINES plain rules at send — a plain canary would lie green
         everywhere. The block's own style element is HOISTED into the head
         stylesheet by EN (measured 2026-08-09), so the canaries share the
         fate of the template CSS they probe. Import-excluded: never ships in
         a real send unless deliberately overridden. Permanent (user decision
         2026-08-18): the instant Gmail-budget diagnostic for any suspect
         send; data-probe keeps its signal colors out of the app's palette
         census and color-usage audit. -->
    <mj-raw><div data-import-exclude="true"></mj-raw>
    <mj-section css-class="block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px" data-probe>
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;">PROBE — head CSS canary (dev block; exclude from real sends)</p>
          <p style="font-size:12px;">Bar 1 GREEN = this client applied the head stylesheet, RED = dropped it (the Gmail-app size cliff). Bar 2 BLUE only under 600px. Bar 3 PURPLE only at 600px and up. Bar 4 WHITE-ON-BLACK only in dark mode.</p>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-raw><style>
@media only screen and (max-width: 9999px) {
  .probe-canary-head { background-color: #1a7a1a !important; }
}
@media only screen and (max-width: 599px) {
  .probe-canary-mobile { background-color: #1d4ed8 !important; }
}
@media only screen and (min-width: 600px) {
  .probe-canary-desktop { background-color: #6b21a8 !important; }
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  .probe-canary-dark { background-color: #000000 !important; color: #ffffff !important; }
}
</style></mj-raw>
        <mj-raw><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr><td class="probe-canary-head" style="background-color:#b91c1c;color:#ffffff;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;padding:10px 12px;">1 &mdash; HEAD CSS: green applied / red dropped</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-size:4px;line-height:4px;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="probe-canary-mobile" style="background-color:#9ca3af;color:#ffffff;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;padding:10px 12px;">2 &mdash; MOBILE RULES: blue under 600px / gray otherwise</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-size:4px;line-height:4px;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="probe-canary-desktop" style="background-color:#9ca3af;color:#ffffff;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;padding:10px 12px;">3 &mdash; DESKTOP RULES: purple at 600px+ / gray otherwise</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-size:4px;line-height:4px;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="probe-canary-dark" style="background-color:#f3f4f6;color:#362229;font-family:Tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;padding:10px 12px;">4 &mdash; DARK BRANCH: white-on-black in dark mode / light otherwise</td></tr>
</table></mj-raw>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-raw></div></mj-raw>
    <!-- END: Probe Block (head CSS canary) -->
